 ### 6. Post-Processing Callbacks
 
-**Purpose**: Apply additional transformations after initial configuration processing.
+**Purpose**: Apply additional transformations at well-defined points in the pipeline.
 
 - **Implementation**:
-  - A list of functions or methods called after the driver rules are applied, enabling custom logic specific to the platform.
+  - `post_load_callbacks`: a list of functions called after a config finishes parsing (`get_hconfig`/`get_hconfig_fast_load`), enabling custom load-time normalization specific to the platform (e.g. Cisco IOS folding a wrapped `switchport trunk allowed vlan ... add ...` continuation line back into one canonical line before any diff runs).
+  - `post_remediation_callbacks`: a list of functions called after `config_to_get_to()` computes a remediation or rollback diff, enabling custom rewriting of the computed commands (e.g. Cisco IOS rewriting a full trunk-vlan negate-and-reapply pair into an `add`/`remove` delta).
 
